/* ============================================================
   CONTESTED LANE BLEND — middle colour is a real colour-mix of
   player + enemy via additive RGB averaging. The visible result
   tracks color theory:
     • cyan (player default) + red (enemy)  → magenta/purple
     • green theme           + red          → yellow-gold
     • gold theme            + red          → orange
     • silver theme          + red          → muted pink-rose
     • purple theme          + red          → red-violet
   Both halves stay distinct in their own halves of the lane;
   the mix only emerges at the centerline where the two sides
   physically meet. User spec: "color theory and a cool little
   mechanic — implement it like a professional game dev."
   ============================================================ */
/* Theme-aware contested lane chrome. The centerline + middle circle
   compute their colors as the LIVE color-mix of AI red and the
   player's current theme accent. So the seam reads as:
     player cyan   + AI red → purple/violet
     player white  + AI red → pink         (silver theme)
     player gold   + AI red → orange
     player green  + AI red → muddy ochre
     player purple + AI red → red-violet
   User direction: "It doesn't make sense for the lane to be blue when
   the player is white. White and red make pink in the middle.
   Everything has to be unique to each neon highlight."
   Defines a per-lane CSS variable --contest-mix once, then both
   surfaces (sep::before bar + lane-number circle) derive from it
   with brightness-shifted variants. */
/* Contested centerline + middle circle now use var(--contest-pop) —
   the hand-picked vivid neon set per theme on body. Each theme picks
   its OWN saturated mid color (silver→hot pink, gold→orange,
   green→yellow, etc.) so the seam never desaturates. */
.lane.occ-both .lane-sep::before {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg,
    transparent 0%,
    var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)) 8%,
    var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)) 92%,
    transparent 100%) !important;
  box-shadow:
    0 0 14px var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)),
    0 0 32px var(--contest-pop-soft, rgba(255, 60, 200, 0.55)),
    0 0 56px var(--contest-pop-soft, rgba(255, 60, 200, 0.25)) !important;
}
.lane.occ-both .lane-number {
  border-color: var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)) !important;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)) 40%, white) !important;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)) 18%, rgba(0,0,0,0.85)) !important;
  box-shadow:
    0 0 14px var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)),
    0 0 28px var(--contest-pop-soft, rgba(255, 60, 200, 0.45)),
    inset 0 0 6px color-mix(in srgb, var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200)) 20%, transparent) !important;
  text-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--contest-pop, rgb(255, 60, 200));
}

/* AI mini-hand card-backs — enemy theme (was hardcoded red). */
.ai-hand-mini .card-back {
